mantle rm398
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for cty_vesper_greenholt
title the stormless shelf
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=woodcutter
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk straightens_one_shelf_each_time_a_storm_costs_an_hours_sleep
likes roast_pork digging tidy_house summer_evenings
dislikes cold_tea haggling
fears having_to_start_the_road_empty_again
hopes a_warm_board_under_another_tired_traveller
topics weather +0.6 home +0.5 work +0.4 travel +0.3
styles comfort=sheltering gossip=plain refuse=kind tease=none
marks oath saying
persona persona #self.first# uses sleepless hours before storms to put a small home in order and never forgets the first empty arrival at its door.

words
oath! = Tilt my clean shelf | Hollow my chopping block
saying! = The storm may have the sky but not this shelf | A straight stack makes a small house roomy
shelf = the level board | a narrow shelf
wood = a sound billet | a straight stick
block = the heavy block | a flat chopping stump
dig = a spade cut | a deep notch of soil
pot = a lidded crock | a clean pot
tea = a warm cup | a fresh mug
meat = the browned corner | a slice of pork
chair = my sound stool | a plain wooden chair
bark = a strip of bark | a long peel
spade = a steel spade | a sharp digging blade
sky = a low grey lid | a brooding sky
bundle = a snug armload | a balanced bundle
rainnoise = the first drumming | the roof chatter

any
opinion strangers for 2 : I know the price of an arrival carrying nothing. A board to sit on buys a lot of courage for the following day.
opinion road for 1 : A road brought me within reach of a life I could put together with both paws.
opinion dole for 2 : There was a time I'd have called one bowl a year's worth of good fortune.
opinion houses mixed 1 : I'd sooner inspect a plain shelf built square than a whole fine roof in somebody's name.
opinion merchants mixed 1 : Let me see the wood, name the charge, and give me time to judge the two together.
opinion sump for 1 : The little rooms people make comfortable tell you more about a city than the view above its roofs.

grown
line greet : Find a dry spot on the board and sit. | You're welcome beside my working coat.
line greet.return : That greeting has a proper warm place here.
line again.open : Back on the same plank before it cooled.
line farewell : Get where the roof suits the weather. | Carry one good bit of this hour away.
line farewell.return : A level floor and a kind voice at your next stop.
line react.news : Tell me while the wood's settled. | I'll stay steady for the whole account.
line react.news.new : First chip cut from that news for me.
line react.news.known : I remember the grain in that telling.
line react.news.doubt : I would look again before putting a weight on it.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : A wolf in that sort of hurt deserves company through the long hours.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : That's a bright window opened on an ordinary day.
line ask.how : How has your own roof held today?
line answer.how : Sleep's a bit scant. Still enough shoulder for a fair turn.
line sympathise : Here's a seat that doesn't ask you to explain yourself.
line reassure : You can lay the first board and leave the rest till morning.
line refuse : My next bit of strength is promised to another job.
line accept_decline : We'll let that rest in its own quiet corner.
line preclose : Best be off before my homeward strip of light goes.
line accept_preclose : Get to your own warm room while it still feels near.
line ack : I hear just where the grain changes.

scene exchange1
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I wake before the storm has knocked. | If I can't settle before thunder I straighten a shelf.
b : Can you hear it? | Does that ward it off?
a : It's the missing quiet I notice, as though the roof's holding its breath. | It gives the morning one dry bit of order.

scene exchange2
when topic=work self.job=woodcutter
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Coppice wood has a bend you have to greet before cutting. | I stack my sound billets facing the air.
b : Can you straighten it? | How can wood face anywhere?
a : Better choose a use that likes a curve. | Turn a split surface outward and watch which one dries first.

scene exchange3
when topic=pastimes self.likes=digging
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I enjoy the pause when a spadeful comes up clean. | I turn the first clod upside down.
b : Admiring the hole? | Always?
a : Admiring a little space I had a paw in making. | Only to learn which way the roots were travelling.

scene exchange4
when topic=food self.likes=roast_pork
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a strip of rind to set beside my potatoes. | A roast sends a great welcome through a small doorway.
b : Saving it for last? | Even to an empty room?
a : Lending a bit of its good smell to the lot. | I usually find somebody's remembered an errand near me.

scene exchange5
when topic=home self.likes=tidy_house
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : An orderly shelf's a whole inch wider than a messy one. | I hang one peg lower for tired arms.
b : You measured it? | Just for visitors?
a : The last pot fits. That's measure enough. | I've walked plenty far enough to be my own tired visitor.

scene exchange6
when topic=season self.likes=summer_evenings
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Summer light reaches the far end of my shelf. | I like long evenings after a clean day's cutting.
b : What lives there? | More time for the chopping block?
a : The cup I couldn't bear to throw out while I owned just the one. | More time for ordinary company before sleep.

scene exchange7
when topic=food self.dislikes=cold_tea
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I come back to cold tea with a stick in each paw. | I take tea warm with both hands round it.
b : Too busy carrying wood? | To keep it from cooling?
a : Too hopeful about what a mug can do unassisted. | To keep me from starting something else first.

scene exchange8
when topic=prices self.dislikes=haggling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a price you can lay flat on a table. | I'll tell you why a twisted branch costs less.
b : Does haggling curl it up? | Why not bargain it up?
a : It gives it so many corners neither wolf knows what was meant. | A bent stick wants a different job. That's sufficient explanation.

scene exchange9
when topic=family self.married=yes self.spouse
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep a shelf end clear for #self.spouse#. | A roof can sound much calmer with #self.spouse# beside me.
b : A private bit of space? | Even when a storm's near?
a : Every shared house wants a few small places where one voice chooses. | Even when I expect a poor night's rest, the waiting isn't lonely.

scene exchange10
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I came up the road with my paws empty. | The first piece of my own furniture scarcely qualified.
b : What came in first? | Was it a rough chair?
a : A plain pot. There's something hopeful about buying the means of making a meal. | A block to sit on. I owned the whole broad top of it.

scene exchange11
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd put the chair with the stout repair out for #self.friend#. | A friend gets the protected corner by my back step.
b : You'd choose the mended one? | Will you get wet?
a : Because I know each joint and trust it with somebody I care for. | I keep an extra folded cloth. Sharing the place means preparing for both.

scene exchange12
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A city window with two rows of pots always stops me. | I like seeing timber used twice.
b : What are you looking at? | Where does that show?
a : How much home can be made from a small stretch of wall. | Peg holes in a lintel where it once carried a shelf.

scene exchange13
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Here's what drifted in from outside. #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. | A story has a fresh-cut smell when it's truly new.
b : How sound is that account? | And when it's old?
a : I wouldn't use loose bark to hold up a roof. I'd wait to learn more. | You can still see where it's been trimmed to fit the next door.

scene exchange14
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Hard days make me glad of a tidy store of kindling. | A tight spell makes me look at what's still standing.
b : For your own hearth? | Why?
a : And a little armful for a visitor with no dry start. | A decent shelf can outlast a surprisingly poor season.

scene exchange15
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like the first wolf coming up that road empty to see a light. | I want one fine calm night before the weather breaks.
b : What can you offer? | Would a calm night suit you?
a : A board, a dry cloth, something warming while the feet rest. | Lie perfectly still and enjoy the untidiness of the shelf.

scene exchange16
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I shoulder a heavy piece on the smooth side. | I work more slowly after a sleepless night.
b : Wouldn't the bark stop it slipping? | Do you lose a lot of ground?
a : I can steady weight. I don't want to spend the night picking splinters out. | Less than I'd waste rushing a tired cut.

scene exchange17
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I sweep the floor towards the open air after cutting. | I swap my wet outdoor cloth for a dry one as soon as I enter.
b : Does the dust all go? | Why so quickly?
a : I take the answer I can get today. | It tells my shoulders the work journey's finished.

scene exchange18
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can name a road by its places to sit. | I leave a sound block beside paths where I stack wood.
b : Not by the turns? | A seat for you?
a : A tired newcomer looks at a different sort of map. | My legs may be elsewhere when another wolf needs it first.

story tale1 [topic=memories]
  : I started my first night under a roof by lining up every possession I had. It came to one cup and a scrap of cloth.
  : The shelf looked bare enough to make a heart sink, until I put my cup right in the middle.
  b : What difference did the middle make?
  : I could choose it. I lived a long time away from places where the position of a cup was mine to decide.

story tale2 [topic=work self.job=woodcutter]
  : I cut a forked branch that looked ideal for a peg. I trimmed the fork neatly, held it against the wall and discovered both ends pointed the same way.
  : A coat would slide off either prong before I got my arms out.
  b : Was the fork still useful?
  : I made it a wooden bird and turned its useless pegs into excellent wings. It lives above the sound coat hook.

story tale3 [topic=weather]
  : One sleepless night I made up my mind to sort the jars by height. The first thunder came while I was still standing the second tallest beside the third.
  : I woke in the chair after sunrise with a little jar balanced on each knee.
  b : Was your shelf properly arranged?
  : Mostly. I put the two little ones side by side, made my tea and kept the chair in its comfortable place.

rule @call1
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=woodcutter
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Split the piece where the grain invites it. | Bark down on the damp side of the pile.

rule @call2
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Summer light or winter, there's a welcome on a cleaned board. | An evening needs a place to put a cup.

rule @call3
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The roof has finally said what it was brooding over. | A sound shelf for the jars to wait on.

rule @call4
when concept=bark self.likes=digging
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One good spadeful and a neat place for the next. | Roots still show the way their rain went.
dlg resident.hub : There's a sound seat here, built to have company on it.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, you're as welcome as warm tea when the day's cutting is over.
dlg resident.hub [here.time=night] : A late visitor doesn't trouble me. I have practice with wakeful hours.
dlg resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : We can speak civilly from either end of a level board.
dlg resident.job [self.job=woodcutter] : I cut coppice wood. I like finding a good use even for the little forks.
dlg resident.job : My work buys me the right to come home and hang things where I choose.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : The bit of news that came in from the road was #world.news#.
dlg resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : Talk runs that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. It hasn't had a fair test of its joints.
dlg resident.bye : A warm board beside a sound roof when you next rest.

graft resident.hub
choice Why sort a shelf when a storm's coming? -> night_shelf
node night_shelf
say I'm going to be awake anyway. I'd like the worry to leave something better behind than an early yawn.
free
choice Does the shelf stay tidy? -> night_shelf_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node night_shelf_again
say Until breakfast. A shelf that stays perfect all day probably hasn't got a household to look after.
choice Leave the cup somewhere warm. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
